Acts: [Accept bet, Reject bet];
States: [Heads (p=0.5), Tails (p=0.5)];
Payoffs (if Accept): Heads = +G gold, Tails = -30 gold;
Utility (risk‑neutral, CRRA with exponent 0.5 for illustration): v(g) = sqrt(g) for gains, v(-l) = -λ·sqrt(l) for losses.
Indifference condition: 0.5·sqrt(G) = 0.5·λ·sqrt(30) ⇒ sqrt(G) = λ·sqrt(30) ⇒ G = λ²·30.
With λ≈2.25, G ≈ (2.25)²·30 ≈ 5.0625·30 ≈ 151.9 ≈ 152 gold.
Thus a loss‑averse individual expects roughly 150 gold to feel indifferent.

